{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-46932","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88347","text":"Slice B, Commit 3 — the "},{"id":"spn-88348","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-88349","text":" surface: closure memo"}]},{"id":"blk-46933","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88350","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status:"},{"id":"spn-88351","text":" CLOSED. "},{"id":"spn-88352","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run48"},{"id":"spn-88353","text":" PASS_REF_AND_NATIVE (6s, 71 rows). "},{"id":"spn-88354","marks":["code"],"text":"mutate48"},{"id":"spn-88355","text":" "},{"id":"spn-88356","marks":["bold"],"text":"19/19 ALL CAUGHT"},{"id":"spn-88357","text":". Full sweep "},{"id":"spn-88358","marks":["code"],"text":"run_l0_sweep"},{"id":"spn-88359","text":" "},{"id":"spn-88360","marks":["bold"],"text":"16/16 green"},{"id":"spn-88361","text":" (141s, reference + native), L-0 tier unmoved."}]},{"id":"blk-46934","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88362","text":"Commit 2 gave a route a canonical form and an identity but no spelling. Commit 3 gives it the ruled spelling in both directions:"}]},{"id":"blk-46935","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"[p0] ~~msg~~> [mb] (body=0.0.0.7)"},{"id":"blk-46936","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88363","text":"and closes the two things that spelling makes reachable — the Q4 writer-15 reservation, and a silent world substitution in the authoring draft."}]},{"id":"blk-46937","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88364","text":"1. What shipped"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-46939","spans":[{"id":"spn-88365","text":"file"}]},{"id":"blk-46940","spans":[{"id":"spn-88366","text":"change"}]}],"id":"blk-46938","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-46941","spans":[{"id":"spn-88367","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_ir.py"}]},{"id":"blk-46942","spans":[{"id":"spn-88368","marks":["code"],"text":"_ROUTE_RE"},{"id":"spn-88369","text":", "},{"id":"spn-88370","marks":["code"],"text":"_ROUTE_KEYS"},{"id":"spn-88371","text":", "},{"id":"spn-88372","marks":["code"],"text":"_body_dots"},{"id":"spn-88373","text":", the route branch in "},{"id":"spn-88374","marks":["code"],"text":"_parse_core_permissive"},{"id":"spn-88375","text":"; bootstrap "},{"id":"spn-88376","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-88377","text":" message split off from "},{"id":"spn-88378","marks":["code"],"text":"!!"},{"id":"spn-88379","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-88380","marks":["code"],"text":"=="}]}],[{"id":"blk-46943","spans":[{"id":"spn-88381","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_format.py"}]},{"id":"blk-46944","spans":[{"id":"spn-88382","text":"route section emitted after the edges, "},{"id":"spn-88383","marks":["code"],"text":"_emit_body"}]}],[{"id":"blk-46945","spans":[{"id":"spn-88384","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_canonical.py"}]},{"id":"blk-46946","spans":[{"id":"spn-88385","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_ROUTE_WRITER_RESERVED"},{"id":"spn-88386","text":", "},{"id":"spn-88387","marks":["code"],"text":"routes_of_artifact"}]}],[{"id":"blk-46947","spans":[{"id":"spn-88388","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_scenario.py"}]},{"id":"blk-46948","spans":[{"id":"spn-88389","marks":["code"],"text":"check_route_writer_reservation"},{"id":"spn-88390","text":", "},{"id":"spn-88391","marks":["code"],"text":"check_world_compatibility"}]}],[{"id":"blk-46949","spans":[{"id":"spn-88392","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_draft.py"}]},{"id":"blk-46950","spans":[{"id":"spn-88393","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_DRAFT_LOSSY_WORLD"},{"id":"spn-88394","text":", the computed "},{"id":"spn-88395","marks":["code"],"text":"_draft_loss"},{"id":"spn-88396","text":" round-trip, both draft doors"}]}],[{"id":"blk-46951","spans":[{"id":"spn-88397","marks":["code"],"text":"spinner_bench.py"}]},{"id":"blk-46952","spans":[{"id":"spn-88398","text":"call site widened to the composed door"}]}],[{"id":"blk-46953","spans":[{"id":"spn-88399","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run47.py"}]},{"id":"blk-46954","spans":[{"id":"spn-88400","text":"closing NOTE corrected (it said \"there is no "},{"id":"spn-88401","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-88402","text":" surface\")"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-46955","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88403","text":"The parser's job stops at "},{"id":"spn-88404","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"this line says a route.\""},{"id":"spn-88405","text":" Endpoint roles, the one-shot source law, the body range, duplicates and the budget are all the seal's, and they are the seal's for a route arriving from "},{"id":"spn-88406","marks":["bold"],"text":"any"},{"id":"spn-88407","text":" surface. Every Q7 row proves this twice: the parse "},{"id":"spn-88408","marks":["bold"],"text":"succeeds"},{"id":"spn-88409","text":" and the seal "},{"id":"spn-88410","marks":["bold"],"text":"refuses"},{"id":"spn-88411","text":". A parser that had helpfully re-implemented one of these fails the first half."}]},{"id":"blk-46956","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88412","text":"2. Five autonomous decisions — please confirm or overrule"}]},{"id":"blk-46957","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88413","text":"(a) The draft "},{"id":"spn-88414","marks":["bold"],"text":"REFUSES"},{"id":"spn-88415","text":" route-bearing worlds rather than being widened"}]},{"id":"blk-46958","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88416","text":"A "},{"id":"spn-88417","marks":["code"],"text":"WorldDraft"},{"id":"spn-88418","text":" stores a world as "},{"id":"spn-88419","marks":["code"],"text":"(objects, edges)"},{"id":"spn-88420","text":". A route is neither, so it was invisible. "},{"id":"spn-88421","marks":["bold"],"text":"Measured before the guard was written:"},{"id":"spn-88422","text":" opening the one-route world for editing produced no error and yielded "},{"id":"spn-88423","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-d3e555be…"},{"id":"spn-88424","text":" — the route-free twin, a perfectly good world with a perfectly good id. Legal, which is what makes it dangerous."}]},{"id":"blk-46959","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88425","text":"Widening the draft to carry routes is not a language change: it is a new revision of "},{"id":"spn-88426","marks":["bold"],"text":"every persisted authoring document"},{"id":"spn-88427","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-88428","marks":["code"],"text":"ForgeProjectV2"},{"id":"spn-88429","text":", the v0.6-0 recovery journal, the draft-state ledger, the canvas reconciler. That is a document-format migration and it does not belong inside a language slice, so commit 3 ships a "},{"id":"spn-88430","marks":["bold"],"text":"refusal"},{"id":"spn-88431","text":" and defers the widening."}]},{"id":"blk-46960","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88432","text":"The guard is a "},{"id":"spn-88433","marks":["bold"],"text":"computed round-trip"},{"id":"spn-88434","text":", not a construct blacklist:"}]},{"id":"blk-46961","kind":"code","language":"python","text":"want = W.lower_graph(g).semantic_artifact_id\ngot, err = _seal(objects, edges, profile)\nif err is None and got == want: return None      # nothing was lost"},{"id":"blk-46962","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88435","text":"It names no construct, so it will refuse the "},{"id":"spn-88436","marks":["italic"],"text":"next"},{"id":"spn-88437","text":" unrepresentable construct without being edited — the same property that made "},{"id":"spn-88438","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_legacy.export_canvas_graph_v1"},{"id":"spn-88439","text":" learn about routes on its own."}]},{"id":"blk-46963","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88440","text":"(b) The loss refusal reports "},{"id":"spn-88441","marks":["code"],"text":"syntax_error"}]},{"id":"blk-46964","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88442","marks":["code"],"text":"REPLACE_STATUS"},{"id":"spn-88443","text":" has four frozen terminal values. "},{"id":"spn-88444","marks":["code"],"text":"syntax_error"},{"id":"spn-88445","text":" is the only one whose "},{"id":"spn-88446","marks":["bold"],"text":"behaviour"},{"id":"spn-88447","text":" is exactly this case (refused, draft untouched, nothing for the author to repair). It is an imperfect "},{"id":"spn-88448","marks":["italic"],"text":"name"},{"id":"spn-88449","text":"; the diagnostic carries the honest code "},{"id":"spn-88450","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_DRAFT_LOSSY_WORLD"},{"id":"spn-88451","text":". Inventing a fifth status is a change to a published contract, not a language decision — hence the deferral."}]},{"id":"blk-46965","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88452","text":"(c) Routes emit "},{"id":"spn-88453","marks":["bold"],"text":"after"},{"id":"spn-88454","text":" the edges, not interleaved"}]},{"id":"blk-46966","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88455","text":"Sorting a route into edge order would need one comparison key spanning two vocabularies, and the two orderings are canonical for different reasons: an edge's order is "},{"id":"spn-88456","marks":["bold"],"text":"presentational"},{"id":"spn-88457","text":", a route's order "},{"id":"spn-88458","marks":["bold"],"text":"IS its minted ADMIT `sequence`"},{"id":"spn-88459","text":" (Q4). Interleaving would make an identity-bearing order look like a formatting choice. A route-free world therefore emits "},{"id":"spn-88460","marks":["italic"],"text":"exactly"},{"id":"spn-88461","text":" the pre-Slice-B text — no separator, no empty section (proved by "},{"id":"spn-88462","marks":["code"],"text":"Q5d"},{"id":"spn-88463","text":", see §3)."}]},{"id":"blk-46967","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88464","text":"(d) "},{"id":"spn-88465","marks":["code"],"text":"check_world_compatibility"},{"id":"spn-88466","text":" composes binding + reservation into one door"}]},{"id":"blk-46968","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88467","text":"Both halves stay callable by name, but production goes through the composed door, because the failure mode of two independent checks is that a call site grows one and not the other — and the forgotten half is whichever was added second. Today that is the reservation. "},{"id":"spn-88468","marks":["code"],"text":"Q8i"},{"id":"spn-88469","text":" and mutation "},{"id":"spn-88470","marks":["bold"],"text":"M16"},{"id":"spn-88471","text":" are the rows that hold this."}]},{"id":"blk-46969","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88472","text":"(e) The bootstrap DSL gets "},{"id":"spn-88473","marks":["bold"],"text":"no"},{"id":"spn-88474","text":" route directive"}]},{"id":"blk-46970","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88475","text":"It is a frozen migration bridge. Its "},{"id":"spn-88476","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-88477","text":" rejection was corrected, though: it used to say "},{"id":"spn-88478","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"a transition class, not an IR v1 edge\""},{"id":"spn-88479","text":", which is now false twice over — a route "},{"id":"spn-88480","marks":["bold"],"text":"is"},{"id":"spn-88481","text":" an IR v1.1 construct, and it was never an edge (D8). It now points at the surface that does have one. "},{"id":"spn-88482","marks":["code"],"text":"!!"},{"id":"spn-88483","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-88484","marks":["code"],"text":"=="},{"id":"spn-88485","text":" keep the old message. This is the identical correction commit 1 made for "},{"id":"spn-88486","marks":["code"],"text":"mailbox"},{"id":"spn-88487","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-46971","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88488","text":"3. What the mutation round found"}]},{"id":"blk-46972","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88489","text":"Three survivors on the first pass, all three real. Recorded because they are the useful part."}]},{"id":"blk-46973","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88490","marks":["bold"],"text":"M9 — the route separator emitted unconditionally. SURVIVED with nothing red."},{"id":"spn-88491","text":" The most useful finding. Whitespace is non-semantic, so no identity moved and "},{"id":"spn-88492","marks":["code"],"text":"Q5"},{"id":"spn-88493","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-88494","marks":["code"],"text":"Q5b"},{"id":"spn-88495","text":" stayed green. And the formatter is "},{"id":"spn-88496","marks":["code"],"text":"graph -> text"},{"id":"spn-88497","text":", not "},{"id":"spn-88498","marks":["code"],"text":"text -> text"},{"id":"spn-88499","text":", so the extra blank line is a "},{"id":"spn-88500","marks":["bold"],"text":"fixed point"},{"id":"spn-88501","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-88502","marks":["code"],"text":"Q3b"},{"id":"spn-88503","text":" (idempotence) stayed green too; the prediction that it would catch this was simply wrong. Meanwhile the canonical "},{"id":"spn-88504","marks":["bold"],"text":"bytes"},{"id":"spn-88505","text":" of every route-free world in the tree had moved — the exact law "},{"id":"spn-88506","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_format"},{"id":"spn-88507","text":"'s own comment claims (\"no blank separator, no empty section\") and which nothing checked. "},{"id":"spn-88508","marks":["bold"],"text":"`Q5d` exists because of this line"},{"id":"spn-88509","text":", and states the law structurally (a route-free world's text ends at its last edge) rather than pinning a literal, which would fork the emitter."}]},{"id":"blk-46974","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88510","marks":["bold"],"text":"M11 — `replace_world_source`'s guard removed. `Q9e` stayed green."},{"id":"spn-88511","text":" "},{"id":"spn-88512","marks":["code"],"text":"Q9e"},{"id":"spn-88513","text":" claims \"the draft is UNTOUCHED\". True, but for the wrong reason: the route-free twin of that source "},{"id":"spn-88514","marks":["italic"],"text":"is"},{"id":"spn-88515","text":" the draft's current world, so a missing guard falls through to the semantic-noop branch and leaves revision 0 with the right candidate. "},{"id":"spn-88516","marks":["code"],"text":"Q9e"},{"id":"spn-88517","text":" is structurally unable to tell "},{"id":"spn-88518","marks":["italic"],"text":"refused"},{"id":"spn-88519","text":" from "},{"id":"spn-88520","marks":["italic"],"text":"silently accepted as a no-op"},{"id":"spn-88521","text":". "},{"id":"spn-88522","marks":["bold"],"text":"`Q9h`/`Q9i`/`Q9j` were added"},{"id":"spn-88523","text":": a paste whose lost world is a "},{"id":"spn-88524","marks":["bold"],"text":"different"},{"id":"spn-88525","text":" world (two mailboxes + a route), plus a vacuity check that the twin really does differ."}]},{"id":"blk-46975","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88526","marks":["bold"],"text":"M14 — the reservation widened to every world. Reported as \"Q8 raised\"."},{"id":"spn-88527","text":" Not a production defect but a reporting one: "},{"id":"spn-88528","marks":["code"],"text":"Q8b"},{"id":"spn-88529","text":" raised, and "},{"id":"spn-88530","marks":["code"],"text":"section()"},{"id":"spn-88531","text":" renamed the failure after its neighbour — so a reservation made too "},{"id":"spn-88532","marks":["bold"],"text":"strong"},{"id":"spn-88533","text":" read as a reservation that was "},{"id":"spn-88534","marks":["bold"],"text":"broken"},{"id":"spn-88535","text":". "},{"id":"spn-88536","marks":["code"],"text":"Q8b"},{"id":"spn-88537","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-88538","marks":["code"],"text":"Q8c"},{"id":"spn-88539","text":" are callables now and keep their own names. (This is the same lesson as run47's \"many laws share one error code\": a row must be identifiable as itself when it fails.)"}]},{"id":"blk-46976","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88540","text":"Also worth recording: "},{"id":"spn-88541","marks":["bold"],"text":"M5"},{"id":"spn-88542","text":" (body arity forked onto "},{"id":"spn-88543","marks":["code"],"text":"_rotor_dots"},{"id":"spn-88544","text":") is caught only at section granularity, and "},{"id":"spn-88545","marks":["code"],"text":"Q1d"},{"id":"spn-88546","text":" cannot see it at all — the rotor message happens to contain the same "},{"id":"spn-88547","marks":["code"],"text":"\"must have 4 lanes\""},{"id":"spn-88548","text":" while saying "},{"id":"spn-88549","marks":["italic"],"text":"rotor"},{"id":"spn-88550","text":" about a "},{"id":"spn-88551","marks":["italic"],"text":"body"},{"id":"spn-88552","text":". That is exactly the drift "},{"id":"spn-88553","marks":["code"],"text":"_body_dots"},{"id":"spn-88554","text":"'s docstring refuses, and it is why the two 4s are not one constant."}]},{"id":"blk-46977","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88555","text":"4. Not frozen"}]},{"id":"blk-46978","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88556","text":"A route can now be "},{"id":"spn-88557","marks":["bold"],"text":"written, canonicalized, sealed, formatted, and refused for every reason it should be"},{"id":"spn-88558","text":" — and it still does nothing at runtime. Commit 4 folds it. Freeze the Slice B line after Commit 4, then promote "},{"id":"spn-88559","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-88560","text":" to Grounded in "},{"id":"spn-88561","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_CORE_0.1.md"},{"id":"spn-88562","text":" §14."}]},{"id":"blk-46979","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88563","text":"Carried obligation into Commit 4: unify "},{"id":"spn-88564","marks":["code"],"text":"route_body_in_range"},{"id":"spn-88565","text":" into "},{"id":"spn-88566","marks":["code"],"text":"admit"},{"id":"spn-88567","text":" to remove the fork (the obligation is written into the function's docstring)."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaieraob2hu6vasuhtka2wrfbdd3cdk5245os2hh6ptxoyc6b37h4y2ygq","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}